# Blossoming Tortoise: its trigger also happens whenever it attacks (turn 3: three Islands are milled, one is returned tapped).
# "Land creatures you control get +1/+1" (CR 613.4c): the Mutavault Bot1 returned on turn 1 and animates on turn 3 is a 2/2 plus +1/+1,
# so 3/3, while the Tortoise itself, a creature but not a land, stays 3/3 (it would be 4/4 if it counted). "Activated abilities of lands you control cost {1} less to activate": with nothing else untapped the Mutavault's {1}
# costs {0}, so it does not tap itself to pay and stays untapped. The attacking Tortoise deals 3.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Blossoming Tortoise
Island x4
Mutavault
Plains
Ornithopter
Forest
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Blossoming Tortoise.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Mutavault)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault.Activate(Ability: {1})
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault.Power = 3
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault.Toughness = 3
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mutavault.Tapped = false
? Bot1.Battlefield.Blossoming Tortoise.Power = 3
? Bot1.Battlefield.Blossoming Tortoise.Toughness = 3
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Blossoming Tortoise > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Island)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Tapped = true
Bot1.Library.Count = 10
